=== Cones ===

The male ([[pollen]]) cones are small, on the ends of shoots that die after pollination.<ref name="IDS"/>  The female (seed) [[conifer cone|cones]] are small, typically erect, and take 4–7 months to reach maturity after pollination.<ref name="IDS"/> The seed scales spread apart when mature, allowing the winged seeds, two per scale, to fall out.<ref name="IDS"/> The leaflike [[bract]] scales can be either long and visible (exserted) or short and hidden between the seed scales.<ref name="IDS"/> 

